{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389707-the-dream-flower-a-question-and-an-idea","id":1389707,"title":"The dream flower, a question and an idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-18T11:04:51-07:00","id":1389707,"title":"The dream flower, a question and an idea","content":"Ok so to give you all a little pretext, given the times we are all living in and the stuff the world is going through with this global pandemic. My group wanted me to run this game for them in order for us to have a little escape from real life for a bit each week. Go figure. lol<br /> <br /> So my game is taking place in June, and in it the city the characters are in has fully re-opened but with safety measures in place. But due the the fear that the pandemic has cause around the globe a new wave of nightmares has flooded the Near Dreaming and are even now spilling out into the Autumn World via wild portals in the region around the characters city. It will be up to them to figure out how to put an end to these portals and with the other local Kiths to clean up the town of nightmares.<br /> <br /> However I have been working on an idea....in my mind it has take the form of a plant that has traveled from some place in the Dreaming or other realm. However the plant works a bit like a virus in that it spread by latching onto to a living host and slowly siphoning their soul off into the Dreaming to wander lost forever...leaving a gelatinous husk behind of the mortal. <br /> <br /> However.... I can't quite figure out how the mechanics would work for this plant, given that most chimerical creature and items can't survive long in the mortal world. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:50:14-07:00","id":1389734,"title":"","content":"Chimera do frequently survive long in the mortal world, it is just costly to interact with banal parts of it.<br /> <br /> But this is a marvelous idea. I would treat it like a poison/disease, in that it has long time damaging effects. I would have a roll made, depending on how potent you want the plant daily or weekly or something, using the targets banality + Stamina (or even Willpower or Wits) vs the chimera. Failing causes you to loose willpower points and then dots when out of points. When reduced to zero the host dies and the blossomed flower digests the soul and turns it into Chimera. It\u2019s similar to an idea I had about people that were spontaneously turned into Chimera and everyone that knew them forgot about them, I called them the Mist-Taken. This is a cool idea though and I would use the plants as one of the vectors.<br /> <br /> I would just have the people turned into Chimera, like instead of a wraith(or Keremet). So they keep their mortal stats, maybe translate some key items for them, and depending on how you want to handle it don\u2019t give them any Redes at first or just a handful. But the big thing would be they are fully self aware chimera, like living people but on the chimerical side. But maybe they change/evolve/mutate based off of their new life and environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:26:58-07:00","id":1389755,"title":"","content":"That is a great idea.....oh yeah and the other part is that the very same chimerical plant if ground up and done right can be used as a drug that in essence allows people to see the chimerical. So yeah if left alone the plant over the course of weeks slowly starts turn the person into a chimera themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you, your feedback was invaluable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:35:29-07:00","id":1389757,"title":"","content":"I've already made an illustration of the plant and how it affects creatures, including other chimera.....after all that is how it travels. If there is a way to post photos on here I would show you guys. But I am very new on here and have not figured everything out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}